{
  "_comment": [
    "A curated sample of real DCS `object_type` strings, used by",
    "test_object_model.py::test_coverage_floor_against_real_type_sample to",
    "measure perception.object_model's keyword-table coverage against real",
    "data instead of guessed strings, and to catch a silent regression.",
    "",
    "Each entry's `expected_op_class` is what perception.object_model.profile_for",
    "should currently return for that real type (null means the fallback/",
    "DEFAULT_OP_CLASS case is the *correct*, expected outcome for this type).",
    "",
    "`bucket` classifies *why* -- used to compute a coverage floor on the",
    "bucket that actually matters (`ground`: modern ground units this module",
    "targets) instead of one blended percentage across everything, which is",
    "exactly the metric that hid this module's original ground-unit gap (see",
    "aircraft-layer/research/2026-09-09-object-model-keyword-coverage.md's",
    "Addendum): 'ship' (OP_SHIP, its own already-covered category, not a",
    "'ground unit'); 'air' (aircraft/helicopters/UAVs, deliberately deferred,",
    "must stay at fallback); 'wwii' (ED's 'Old ...'-prefixed reporting names,",
    "deliberately excluded even when a modern-unit keyword like 'truck' would",
    "otherwise catch them -- see object_model.py's WWII-prefix guard); ",
    "'ground_deferred' (real ground/support types this pass deliberately did",
    "not attempt -- towed AA/mortar pieces, SAM systems beyond the one named",
    "in scope (IRIS-T), static structures, airfield support equipment -- must",
    "stay at fallback, not counted toward the 'ground' floor since covering",
    "them was never this pass's goal); 'ground' (modern ground combat",
    "vehicles/systems this module targets -- tanks/IFVs/APCs/SPGs/SPAAG/SAM/",
    "trucks/infantry -- the coverage floor applies to this bucket only).",
    "",
    "Individual type-name strings only (no reporting names, no full extracted",
    "table -- the full table itself is now committed at",
    "src/perception/data/dcs_type_to_reporting_name.tsv) -- see",
    "aircraft-layer/research/2026-09-09-object-model-keyword-coverage.md for",
    "the source (ED's HelperAI_reporting_names.lua, 595 entries total) and",
    "the full coverage numbers this sample was drawn to demonstrate. All 57",
    "real DCS ship object_type values are included here since that set is",
    "small and fully enumerable, not a random sample of it."
  ],
